<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>app.curant.server</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/opt/python@3.12/bin/python3.12</string>
        <string>-u</string>
        <string>/Users/AbhyudayDhundhel/curant/curant-current/server/app.py</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Flask's relative CURANT_DB_PATH default ("curant.db") and
         render_template_string calls both assume the process is running
         from inside server/ , launchd does not cd there on its own, so
         this has to be set explicitly or the customers table ends up
         created in the wrong directory every restart. -->
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/AbhyudayDhundhel/curant/curant-current/server</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/Users/AbhyudayDhundhel/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <!-- Generated once (python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))")
             and baked in here rather than left unset , without a fixed
             value the server invents a new one on every restart (see
             app.py's own warning), which would silently kill every owner
             login session each time launchd restarts this job. -->
        <key>CURANT_SECRET_KEY</key>
        <string>8300364adf4562474260a8108964498425f1bdb23e256a4ec8b7643d279343cf</string>
        <!-- Disables Flask's debug reloader + auto-browser-open , see
             app.py's own comment on why those are wrong for an
             unattended service. -->
        <key>CURANT_SERVER_DEBUG</key>
        <string>false</string>
        <!-- Shared Gmail OAuth client, added 2026-08-14 so /v1/gmail-oauth-config
             can hand this out to any activated customer , see that endpoint's
             docstring in app.py for the full feature. DELIBERATELY left as
             placeholders here, NOT committed as real values , GitHub's own
             push protection caught a first attempt at baking the real
             client_id/secret directly into this tracked file and correctly
             rejected the push (a Google OAuth client secret is a recognized
             credential pattern regardless of "installed app" secrets being
             less sensitive than most). Fill these in on your OWN deployed
             copy at ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.curant.server.plist only ,
             same "no default, filled in locally, never committed" pattern
             as CURANT_ADMIN_PASSWORD/ADMIN_PASSWORD elsewhere in this repo.
             Get the values from Google Cloud Console > APIs & Services >
             Credentials (the same OAuth client you may have already created
             for your own first Gmail connection). -->
        <key>CURANT_GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID</key>
        <string>REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID</string>
        <key>CURANT_GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET</key>
        <string>REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET</string>
        <key>CURANT_GMAIL_OAUTH_PROJECT_ID</key>
        <string>REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_GMAIL_OAUTH_PROJECT_ID</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-server.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/curant-server-error.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
<!--
Install with:
  cp com.curant.server.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
  launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/app.curant.server 2>/dev/null
  launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.curant.server.plist

Check it's running:
  launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/app.curant.server | grep -E "state|program"

This is the local license/billing server (server/app.py) , runs on
127.0.0.1:5050 permanently in the background so the customer dashboard
(/login) and owner dashboard (/owner) are always reachable, and so
curant-cli's periodic status recheck never sees connection-refused.
Logs land at /tmp/curant-server.log and /tmp/curant-server-error.log.
-->
